{"case_id":"C009","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":98,"change_types":["resource-lifetime refactor","internal memory-management change"],"affected_functions":["create_generator","on_generator_dispose","close_file","do_pread","sendvec_update_refcnt","do_multirange_proceed","do_send_file","serve_with_generator","on_handler_dispose"],"reason":"The commit changes internal sendfile-generator ownership from a manual refcount and explicit file-closing paths to shared pool allocation with a disposal callback. It introduces no new entry point, protocol, configuration, initialization requirement, or input constraint. The existing HTTP harness already registers `h2o_file_register` at `/` and supplies arbitrary request bytes through `h2o_http1_accept` or `h2o_http2_accept`, so it continues to exercise static-file requests, methods, headers, ranges, and connection termination that drive the modified lifetime paths.","evidence":["The harness calls `h2o_file_register(h2o_config_register_path(hostconf, \"/\", 0), \"./examples/doc_root\", NULL, NULL, 0)`.","Fuzz input is sent as the complete client request and processed through `h2o_http1_accept` or `h2o_http2_accept`, preserving control over paths, methods, and request headers.","`create_generator` changes from `h2o_mem_alloc_pool` plus manual `refcnt` to `h2o_mem_alloc_shared(..., on_generator_dispose)`.","`sendvec_update_refcnt` replaces manual increments and `do_close` calls with `h2o_mem_addref_shared` and `h2o_mem_release_shared`.","Removed explicit close calls are replaced by `close_file` or shared-object disposal; public file-handler registration and request semantics are unchanged."],"recommended_action":"Keep the existing fuzz harness unchanged; no new setup or input modeling is required for this internal resource-lifetime refactor."}
